      ":question/problem": "Given $\\mathbf{f}(t)=2 t\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t^{2} - 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}+t^{3}\\,\\mathbf{k}$, find $(\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{\\prime}(t).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{\\prime}(t)=\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{f}(t)+\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)=2 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{2} - 1)=4 t \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{3})=3 t^{2} \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t) & =2\\,\\mathbf{i}+4 t\\,\\mathbf{j}+3 t^{2}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2)=0 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(4 t)=4 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{2})=6 t \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =4\\,\\mathbf{j}+6 t\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(0)(2 t)+(4)(2 t^{2} - 1)+(6 t)(t^{3}) \\\\  & =6 t^{4} + 8 t^{2} - 4 \\\\ P_2 & =(2)(2)+(4 t)(4 t)+(3 t^{2})(3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =9 t^{4} + 16 t^{2} + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}\\cdot \\mathbf{f})^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =15 t^{4} + 24 t^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
